948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,3862,3000,18021,400,66,62,17,4779,400,66,62,16,4779,323,400,66,62,15,3,1741,429,198,78045,87,61,18,488,856,61,17,481,220,20,284,320,87,481,220,18,29776,18,488,272,62,17,320,87,481,220,18,29776,17,488,272,62,16,320,87,481,220,18,8,488,272,62,15,7110,60,9885,400,66,62,17,61,17,488,272,62,16,61,17,488,272,62,15,61,17,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThere exist constants $c_2,$ $c_1,$ and $c_0$ such that\n\\[x^3 + x^2 - 5 = (x - 3)^3 + c_2 (x - 3)^2 + c_1 (x - 3) + c_0.\\]Find $c_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"461bdd88a6b14346e3bb9b0a0dd1ab15e81edab6484ecd77a1dde789df9ef4aa"},"seconds":55.43601870536804,"seed":404690983412807125,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to express the polynomial $x^3 + x^2 - 5$ in terms of $(x-3)$. This involves expanding and comparing coefficients with the right-hand side of the given equation.\n\nFirst, let's expand the right-hand side:\n\\[\n(x-3)^3 + c_2 (x-3)^2 + c_1 (x-3) + c_0.\n\\]\n\nWe start by expanding $(x-3)^3$:\n\\[\n(x-3)^3 = x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27.\n\\]\n\nNext, we expand $c_2 (x-3)^2$:\n\\[\nc_2 (x-3)^2 = c_2 (x^2 - 6x + 9) = c_2 x^2 - 6c_2 x + 9c_2.\n\\]\n\nThen, we expand $c_1 (x-3)$:\n\\[\nc_1 (x-3) = c_1 x - 3c_1.\n\\]\n\nCombining all these, the right-hand side becomes:\n\\[\nx^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27 + c_2 x^2 - 6c_2 x + 9c_2 + c_1 x - 3c_1 + c_0.\n\\]\n\nNow, we collect like terms:\n\\[\nx^3 + (c_2 - 9)x^2 + (27 - 6c_2 + c_1)x + (-27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0).\n\\]\n\nWe need this to be equal to the left-hand side polynomial $x^3 + x^2 - 5$. Therefore, we can equate the coefficients of corresponding powers of $x$:\n\\[\nx^3: \\quad 1 = 1,\n\\]\n\\[\nx^2: \\quad 1 = c_2 - 9,\n\\]\n\\[\nx: \\quad 0 = 27 - 6c_2 + c_1,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{constant term:} \\quad -5 = -27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0.\n\\]\n\nFrom the coefficient of $x^2$, we get:\n\\[\nc_2 - 9 = 1 \\implies c_2 = 10.\n\\]\n\nFrom the coefficient of $x$, we get:\n\\[\n27 - 6c_2 + c_1 = 0 \\implies 27 - 6(10) + c_1 = 0 \\implies 27 - 60 + c_1 = 0 \\implies c_1 = 33.\n\\]\n\nFrom the constant term, we get:\n\\[\n-27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0 = -5 \\implies -27 + 9(10) - 3(33) + c_0 = -5 \\implies -27 + 90 - 99 + c_0 = -5 \\implies -36 + c_0 = -5 \\implies c_0 = 31.\n\\]\n\nNow, we have the values of $c_2$, $c_1$, and $c_0$:\n\\[\nc_2 = 10, \\quad c_1 = 33, \\quad c_0 = 31.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find $c_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2$:\n\\[\nc_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2 = 10^2 + 33^2 + 31^2 = 100 + 1089 + 961 = 2150.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2150}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2150}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
